OL,3,GNEWSAYoung adults in the North 'dying
OL,4,Aat higher rates'
OL,5,
OL,6,FYounger adults living in the North of
OL,7,FEngland are 42% more likely to die than
OL,8,Ftheir counterparts in the South,
OL,9,Faccording to new research.
OL,11,FA study by academics in Manchester and
OL,12,FLiverpool found people in the North
OL,13,Faged 25 to 49 faced a significantly
OL,14,Fhigher risk of death than people of the
OL,15,Fsame age living in the South.
OL,17,FResearchers said deprivation was a
OL,18,Fmajor factor behind the gap and called
OL,19,Ffor urgent action to tackle
OL,20,Finequalities.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
